[control-101-a-refusal-the-manifest-made-scores-a-negative-test]
LanguageErrors.MayScore stops asking WHICH refusal happened. Every classified code may answer a negative test, which is the scoring bug this whole path exists to refuse: an engine admitting almost none of the language agrees with a suite whose negative tests all declare a refusal, and the agreement is scored.
exit 3
FAIL only-an-early-error-may-score-and-every-class-is-populated: disagreeing: [NestingTooDeep, ConstructOutsideManifest, AssignmentToConstant, UnresolvableIdentifier, TooManyLocals, TooManyConstants, OperandStackTooDeep]; classes populated: True
