[control-103-a-file-the-harness-declines-is-dropped-rather-than-counted]
The translator returns nothing for a file it cannot run. THE SCORED RUN DOES NOT NOTICE - it reports a clean total over a smaller candidate count - so this is judged by the harness's own checks, which is what they are for.
exit 3
FAIL a-file-this-harness-cannot-run-is-counted-and-named-rather-than-dropped: 6 of 6 were dropped or wrongly selected
broiler-js-conformance: 1 of 42 harness checks FAILED

[control-104-the-strict-reading-is-not-made-strict]
The strict variant is registered under its own name and run without the prologue that makes it strict, so both readings of a file are the same reading twice.
exit 3
FAIL a-file-declaring-no-strictness-becomes-two-cases-and-only-one-carries-the-prologue: 2 cases: a.js#strict, a.js#sloppy
broiler-js-conformance: the harness's own checks failed; nothing was scored

[control-105-the-language-class-map-falls-behind-the-vocabulary]
One code loses its declared class, standing for a code added to the front end and not classified here. The map under-reports rather than inventing passes - the fixture becomes unscorable rather than a pass - and the totality check still fails, because a silent under-report is a defect too.
exit 3
