# Reverting control 108 exposed a defect in the CONTROL DRIVER rather than in the harness: it
# restored its saved copies in forward order, so a file patched twice was rewritten with the state
# after the first patch. It was caught by re-running the harness checks against a known count, and
# the file was restored by hand. Recorded because a control run that quietly leaves an injection
# behind is worse than one that never ran.
